.TH CHTTPSVR_ROUTER_ON_STREAM 3 "2026-07-10" "c_collections" "C Collections Library - Functions"
.SH NAME
chttpsvr_router_on_stream \- register a streaming handler on a sub-router
.SH LIBRARY
C Collections (libccollections, \-lccollections)
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
#include <chttpserver.h>

ccol_retval_t chttpsvr_router_on_stream(chttpsvr_router *router,
                                         chttp_method_t method,
                                         const char *pattern,
                                         chttpsvr_handler_fn fn,
                                         void *ctx);
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
.nf
Same as chttpsvr_register_streaming_handler but registers the route on
a sub-router.  All pattern validation rules from
chttpsvr_register_streaming_handler apply here as well, including the
requirement that pattern begins with '/' and that {name} segments
contain only [A-Za-z0-9_], and support for CHTTP_ANY as the method
argument.
.fi
.SH RETURN VALUE
.nf
ccol_success on success.
ccol_invalid_args if router, pattern, or fn is NULL; if pattern does
                  not begin with '/'; if pattern contains consecutive
                  slashes or a trailing slash; or if a {name} segment
                  contains characters outside [A-Za-z0-9_].
ccol_not_enough_memory if allocation fails.
.fi
.SH "SEE ALSO"
.BR chttpsvr_register_streaming_handler (3),
.BR chttpsvr_subrouter (3)
